Subject: Cantor Deterministic Runtime Activation Plan

@ [plan_uuid] 170ecc4c-762c-4f32-b7f0-002b30fccb14
@ [requirement_set] CDRA-001 through CDRA-040

& [SpecificationPlan] is current
  + preserve and audit inputs
  + explode forty requirements
  + refine terms and data
  + constrain, prune, exhaust, and justify
  + map requirements, register, author canonical, sign, and phase-lock
  + stop before implementation

& [FutureImplementationPlan] is ordered but not currently claimed
  + CDRA-I01 implement pure RuntimeRoot, Operation, Receipt, Fault, bounds, and transition dispatcher over existing temporal forms
  + CDRA-I02 implement FakeRepository and deterministic indexes
  + CDRA-I03 implement LogicalClock, FakeCalendar, recurrence, wake, and DeterministicPlanner
  + CDRA-I04 implement ChangeCapsule, tandem lane, join, barrier, timeout, cancellation, and reentry state machines
  + CDRA-I05 implement bounded compiler forward and independent rear fixtures
  + CDRA-I06 add normalized replay, generative transitions, adversarial negatives, and integration proof
  + CDRA-I07 audit requirement support, effects, bounds, residuals, and release status

& [DependencyAndStopRules] are exact
  + I01 precedes I02 through I05
  + I02 and I03 precede I04 integration
  + I02 through I05 precede I06
  + I06 precedes I07
  + each slice requires a separate claim and completed-work review
  + stop on any need for live effect, persistence, thread, provider, general compiler, model, or hardware behavior

& [VerificationPlan] is proportional
  + canonical serialization and exact-version fixtures
  + legal and illegal state transition tables
  + byte-stable replay
  + bound and resource refusal tests
  + stale, cycle, recurrence, wake, join, barrier, timeout, compiler correspondence, and forbidden-effect negatives
  + full workspace tests with inherited unrelated faults reported separately
